      "body": "## Overview\n\nReturn HTTP 400, not 500, when a chat request carries corrupt audio that libsndfile recognises (for example a truncated WAV).\n\n## Claims\n\n- A truncated or otherwise corrupt-but-recognised `input_audio` / `audio_url` now maps to a 400, as the PyAV path already does.\n\n## Validation\n\n`pytest --noconftest tests/multimodal/media/test_audio.py::test_audio_media_io_rejects_truncated_wav_as_value_error` (CPU, no GPU needed): fails before (`soundfile.LibsndfileError`), passes after. A 30-byte WAV reproduced the 500 through `MediaConnector.fetch_audio` and `create_error_response`. `ruff check` and `ruff format` are clean.\n\n## Details\n\nIn `load_audio`, `except soundfile.LibsndfileError` re-raises any code outside `{0, 1, 3, 4}`. A truncated WAV gives code 71 (\"No 'data' chunk marker\"), and `LibsndfileError` is a `RuntimeError`, so it maps to 500. The branch now raises `ValueError(\"Invalid or corrupted audio data...\") from exc`, like the PyAV branch. The transcription endpoint already wraps this error, so only the chat path was affected.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
